WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:00.800
Thank you.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:42.830
Hey, fellas, give a look. How about that good-bye drink, Jenny?

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:45.440
Why not? One bar's just like another.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:46.600
As long as they got bourbon.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:48.080
Or a reasonable facsimile.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:01:59.480
Bourbon straight with a bourbon chase.

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:00.780
Same.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:03.960
Two separate glasses, get it?

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:05.870
Why wouldn't I get it?

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:14.670
Got that monkey music in here?

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:18.040
Somebody call me a monkey?

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:20.490
Give that thing a rest, will you?

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:22.420
Why don't it's his nickel?

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:31.580
Somebody call me a monkey.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:33.660
Nobody calls nobody nothing.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.000
Just forget it, will you?

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.340
That thing gives me a headache.

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:39.190
Ain't that a pity?

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:06.180
I told you I had a headache.

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:07.790
Put that back, but quick.

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:11.670
You put it back.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:12.880
Why, you...

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:20.200
Steady, corporal.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:20.860
Get out of my way.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.000
I said steady.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:23.620
You didn't get those stripes from blowing your top?

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:24.720
Hey, cut that out.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:25.900
Cut it out, do you hear?

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:28.120
You two guys want to fight so bad,

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:29.320
why don't you get into a uniform?

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:32.090
What do you figure I had on when I got this, huh?

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:33.460
What do you figure?

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:36.640
There's a plate in here as big as your brains, maybe bigger.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:40.540
Well, I don't want no roughhouse in here.

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:43.770
Go on, get back to your bar before you get a face full of knuckles.

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:46.070
Come on, Buzz.

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:50.060
Hey, who's paying for that broken cord?

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:50.920
Save it.

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:52.860
It's long enough you can hang yourself.

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:54.950
Okay, now you got that out of your system.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:56.190
That thing was getting my goat.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:00.940
My mistake, fella.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:02.180
That's okay, skip it.

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:04.190
So long.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:04.780
So long.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:05.400
Bye.

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:09.240
Hey, we better get going, too, if we're gonna catch that bus.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:12.050
Hey, look, Doe, we already caught the bus.

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:17.410
Yeah, that's right, we did, didn't we?

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:19.820
That must be getting dumb.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:22.240
Yes, to you, Johnny.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:23.630
Yeah, you're lucky stiff.

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.050
At least you got a wife to come home to.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:33.620
Boy, if I had a wife and kid to come home to you, what's the matter?

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:37.180
It should be getting old. That stuff kicks me right in the teeth.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.000
When do we get to meet her, Johnny?

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:45.730
Anytime. The door will always be open.

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:48.530
We won't need no dress suit to get in there, will we?

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:52.430
That Cavendish Court hotel and bungalow sounds like a lot of dough.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:53.360
I never...

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:56.380
I, uh, I got a lead on an apartment.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.500
If it comes through, we'll give you a ring.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:04.380
Good. Well, here's to what was.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:18.020
Take care of our boy, George.

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:18.760
You bet I will.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:19.380
See you soon.

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:20.790
Okay.

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:21.980
Johnny.

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:22.780
Yeah?

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:24.940
Did you think you ought to call her before you go home?

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:27.740
Maybe.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:39.120
You don't sound very happy somehow.

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:56.300
Mrs. Morrison, please.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:57.440
What name shall I say?

00:05:58.230 --> 00:05:59.490
Mrs. Morrison is my wife.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:01.780
Yes, sir.

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:04.500
Oh, uh, would you mind if I surprised you?

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:06.000
Oh, no, of course not.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:08.800
Take Mr. Morrison to Bungalow 93.

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:10.660
This way, please.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:11.720
Thank you.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:15.420
Prize is right.

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:17.710
What'd you say, honey?

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:20.020
Nothing to you.

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:38.120
I'll take it from here.

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:03.890
No, I'm afraid not. I'm looking for my wife.

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:07.490
These are four of them, dear.

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:09.300
What's your name, huh?

00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:11.050
Morris.

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:13.050
Does my wife live here?

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:40.900
Relax. Didn't you let me know?

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:42.790
To surprise you.

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:44.780
Take off your coat, Johnny. You're home, you know.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:46.670
A long time, Helen.

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:47.610
Well, much too long.

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:48.900
Well, you're not in uniform.

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:51.270
No, they decided I had enough for a while.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:52.880
They put me on the inactive list.

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:53.490
Oh?

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:55.070
Buzz and George are out, too.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:58.180
Buzz was wounded, and George's eyes went back on him.

00:07:58.520 --> 00:07:59.120
Buzz and George.

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:03.000
I used to write you about them, don't you remember?

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:05.700
Oh, sure. Well, it's great to have you back, Johnny.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:06.960
Come and meet my friends.

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:08.760
Oh, must I now?

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:09.380
Well, certainly.

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:11.740
Dick, hold the piano a while. Hold it.

00:08:11.980 --> 00:08:14.320
Please, everybody, come and meet my husband.

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:17.840
This is Lieutenant Commander John Morrison of the United States Navy.

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:19.240
He's just back in the South Pacific.

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:22.760
Johnny, this is Charlie and Beverly, Rick and Carmen.

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:24.510
Eddie! Eddie!

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:25.910
We're based on Quasley.

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:26.930
What were you flying, sir?

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:27.590
Liberator.

00:08:27.710 --> 00:08:28.130
Excuse me, Dick.

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:29.870
Johnny, this is Eddie Harwood.

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:31.290
I'm glad to know you.

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:32.550
Heard a lot about you.

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:33.900
Guess you might have had a rough time of it.

00:08:34.210 --> 00:08:36.110
I'm afraid my experiences are pretty dull.

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:37.310
I can't believe that.

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:38.820
Hey, wouldn't you like a drink?

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:40.660
Not right now, thanks.

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:42.870
I'd like to get cleaned up a little.

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:44.910
Oh, take your things in there, Johnny.

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:47.170
Excuse me.

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:55.980
I think I'd better breeze.

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:56.420
Why?

00:08:56.620 --> 00:08:58.550
The obvious why.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:19.730
So what pardon me you've got the wrong lipstick on mister

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:33.140
I'm sorry. Forget it.

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:39.820
Ladies and gentlemen, I think you'd better leave.

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:42.000
My husband would like to be alone with me.

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:44.220
He probably wants to beat me up.

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:46.520
Perhaps you want me to apologize.

00:09:47.740 --> 00:09:50.140
Apologize, darling? But you don't have to.

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:53.330
You're a hero. A hero can get away with anything.

00:09:55.910 --> 00:09:57.130
It seems I've lost my manners.

00:09:59.110 --> 00:09:59.970
But would anyone here know that...

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:00.520
Difference

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:45.050
What are you doing?

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:48.180
Get this photograph of Dickie.

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:49.650
I've never seen it before.

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:52.040
Why didn't you send me one?

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:53.640
I thought I had.

00:11:03.770 --> 00:11:08.310
Let's talk this out, Helen. Would you mind not drinking anymore, Justin?

00:11:08.450 --> 00:11:10.050
Oh, for heaven's sakes, don't start preaching.

00:11:12.910 --> 00:11:16.320
I take all the drinks I like, anytime, anyplace.

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:19.400
I go where I want to with anybody I want.

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:22.410
I just happen to be that kind of a girl.

00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:27.500
I thought Dickie's death would have made a little more difference.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:32.560
We lived in a five-room house, and I did the laundry.

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:35.740
And I never went anywhere because I had a kid to look after.

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:39.330
I don't have a kid to look after anymore.

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:45.620
And the people I go with now don't use a kiss as an excuse to sock each other.

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:50.410
Drinking that, you won't need an excuse.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:51.960
Really?

00:11:52.950 --> 00:11:55.950
You are not paying for my drinks.

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:05.450
Well, why don't you answer it? You want to run everything else around here.

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:21.660
Johnny. Oh, hello, Buzz. Got the place, huh?

00:12:22.060 --> 00:12:25.760
Yeah. Yeah, where George lived before. Walked right into it.

00:12:26.950 --> 00:12:29.970
Yeah. And it was 19 guys ahead of us, but they liked George.

00:12:31.030 --> 00:12:34.780
Oh, that's great, Buzz. Hey, uh, what's your telephone number?

00:12:42.060 --> 00:12:42.980
Hillside 8661.

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:44.070
Okay, bye.

00:12:44.230 --> 00:12:51.880
You always found an apartment? Yes.

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:56.830
No, these things were ever blue.

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:59.000
They're Eddie Howard's calling cards.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.000
There's a nightclub on the strip called the Blue Dahlia.

00:13:10.770 --> 00:13:11.890
Let's try just once more.

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:15.750
I'd love to. I'm a girl that tries and tries.

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:20.730
Well, suppose we begin by... You're not drinking anymore.

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:24.270
Suppose we begin by you minding your own business.

00:13:24.770 --> 00:13:25.430
So you've had enough.

00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:26.730
Take your paws off me!

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:32.570
Maybe you've learned to like hurting people.

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:36.720
I could tell you something about Dickie that would hurt you plenty.

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:38.970
What about Dickie?

00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:47.720
I see you in here, aren't you?

00:13:49.450 --> 00:13:49.850
So what?

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:53.200
Call that a prayer meeting?

00:13:54.540 --> 00:13:55.340
Okay, Mr. Morrison.

00:13:56.170 --> 00:13:56.930
You're doing my job.

00:13:57.110 --> 00:13:59.880
If you close up, it's gonna rain.

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:01.370
Okay.

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:03.870
Oh, maybe you'd better pull the blinds down, too,

00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:05.390
if you're gonna push your wife around.

00:14:11.270 --> 00:14:12.390
Call from the house detective.

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:13.870
Pretty, isn't it?

00:14:17.010 --> 00:14:17.850
Now, what about Dickie?

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:19.540
Forget it, Johnny.

00:14:19.720 --> 00:14:20.100
It was nothing.

00:14:20.240 --> 00:14:20.900
What about Dickie?

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:22.690
It was nothing, I tell you.

00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:24.530
Talk! Tell me, will you?

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:25.390
Johnny, please.

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:27.660
It could happen to anybody.

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:28.970
I'd be to a party.

00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:29.970
I had...

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:33.010
to take Dickie with me and a few drinks.

00:14:35.190 --> 00:14:36.270
Oh, stop the tears.

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:39.260
All right, hero.

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:41.740
I was drunk.

00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:43.740
I was in a car smash.

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:46.520
Dickie was killed.

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:50.240
I wrote you he died of diphtheria

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:51.740
because I was afraid to tell you the truth.

00:15:44.780 --> 00:15:58.880
That's what I ought to do, but you're not worth it.

00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:27.160
Line, please.

00:16:29.020 --> 00:16:29.970
York, two...

00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:37.390
8338. Mr. Howard, please. Mrs. Morrison calling.

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:44.700
Will you ask him to call me, please?

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:07.200
Yeah, Johnny. Oh, oh, yeah, Mrs. Morrison.

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:08.620
George and me, we're Johnny's pals.

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:10.650
I know. That's why I'm calling.

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:15.060
We had a quarrel. He walked out on me.

00:17:15.840 --> 00:17:16.500
Walked out on you?

00:17:18.920 --> 00:17:21.800
Well, don't you worry about a thing, George and me.

00:17:21.900 --> 00:17:23.700
We'll bring him back if we have to frog march him.

00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:26.320
Yeah, sure. He'll come over here.

00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:28.530
Yeah, I'll call you as soon as he shows up.

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:30.650
That's all right.

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:36.610
George.

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:38.280
Hey, George.

00:17:38.480 --> 00:17:41.550
That's right.

00:17:41.650 --> 00:17:41.950
He went out.

00:17:51.240 --> 00:17:51.860
Quiet in there.

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:53.020
Quiet!

00:17:53.280 --> 00:17:54.440
We got a sick baby.

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:03.700
We eat eggs.

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:05.620
Johnny's wife just caught up.

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:06.640
Yeah?

00:18:07.880 --> 00:18:08.320
That's swell.

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:09.900
No, it ain't swell.

00:18:10.760 --> 00:18:12.720
He just walked out on her.

00:18:15.910 --> 00:18:16.550
Did you hear from him?

00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:18.120
Not yet.

00:18:19.140 --> 00:18:20.620
He will come over here, though, won't he, George?

00:18:22.050 --> 00:18:22.970
Not if I know him, he won't.

00:18:24.420 --> 00:18:26.040
But I just told his wife we'd bring him back.

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:26.780
What are we gonna do?

00:18:27.450 --> 00:18:29.800
Look, Buzz, there isn't anything we can do.

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:32.680
This is one problem Johnny's got to handle by himself.

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:34.620
Yeah, but if he's not going to...

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:34.900
Forget it.

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:37.720
Whatever's the right thing to do, Johnny will do it.

00:18:41.060 --> 00:18:41.860
We ought to do something.

00:18:43.420 --> 00:18:44.340
We've got to find Johnny.

00:18:44.780 --> 00:18:45.860
Yeah, we'll talk about it afterwards.

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:46.640
Let's eat first.

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:48.100
We've got real eggs.

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:52.330
Come up, will you, while I get the rest of these things ready?

00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:54.140
There's mrs. Morrison who shall I say is calling just say buzz buzz that's my name. Oh 93

00:20:01.310 --> 00:20:02.850
I'm sorry Mrs. Morrison isn't in.

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:05.770
Would you care to leave a message?

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:12.160
Well, you mind if I wait around?

00:20:12.550 --> 00:20:14.300
Not at all. It's over there.

00:20:14.760 --> 00:20:14.960
Huh?

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:16.290
The bar.

00:20:17.580 --> 00:20:18.290
Oh, thank you.

00:20:21.270 --> 00:20:29.820
Uh, bourbon?

00:20:30.030 --> 00:20:36.420
In a minute, meet out the Blue Dahlia the other night.

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:40.670
I may have been there, but we certainly didn't meet.

00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:43.180
Sure, we have mutual friends.

00:20:43.960 --> 00:20:45.220
Hey, you, that's my seat.

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:46.520
Don't pick yourself an orchid.

00:20:50.260 --> 00:20:50.920
Masterful type.

00:20:51.200 --> 00:20:52.680
All I want is a drink and quick.

00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:53.760
Hey, how about that?

00:20:54.710 --> 00:20:55.450
Take one of mine.

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:17.670
Scotch so they tell me i'll buy you a drink some rainy night it's raining now

00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:27.540
right i'll buy you a drink and no passes

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:32.440
What's the matter, don't you believe me?

00:21:33.670 --> 00:21:37.130
Okay, so I won't buy you a drink.

00:21:38.600 --> 00:21:41.530
That's the end of that conversation.

00:21:42.170 --> 00:21:44.520
Wait a minute, you can buy me a drink.

00:21:45.980 --> 00:21:48.220
Only not in this joint. I've had enough of it.

00:21:57.180 --> 00:21:59.490
Really coming down now. We haven't far to go.

00:22:00.440 --> 00:22:04.770
Look, you don't want to go out, Nat. Why don't we go back to the bar?

00:22:05.730 --> 00:22:08.710
Anyway, I came here to see somebody, and I ought to stick around until she gets here.

00:22:09.470 --> 00:22:11.710
Well, you can phone from my place and leave word where you are.

00:22:12.120 --> 00:22:12.660
You live here?

00:22:13.020 --> 00:22:14.570
Sure. Come on.

00:22:19.500 --> 00:22:21.110
What's the matter? Scared?

00:22:25.740 --> 00:22:26.900
Sorry. No pick-up tonight.

00:22:48.940 --> 00:22:49.880
Good evening, Mr. Harwood.

00:22:49.980 --> 00:22:50.620
Good evening, Noli.

00:22:50.980 --> 00:22:52.040
Kind of wet out, isn't it?

00:22:52.720 --> 00:22:53.620
It certainly is.

00:23:00.860 --> 00:23:01.400
Hello, Eddie.

00:23:02.390 --> 00:23:02.810
You're early.

00:23:04.410 --> 00:23:05.270
Evening, Leo. How's everything?

00:23:05.880 --> 00:23:07.180
Took in seven grand last week.

00:23:08.010 --> 00:23:08.490
That's fine.

00:23:09.470 --> 00:23:09.910
Have a drink?

00:23:11.300 --> 00:23:11.680
No, thanks.

00:23:12.500 --> 00:23:13.180
Home tonight, huh?

00:23:18.310 --> 00:23:20.230
That Morrison thing was getting to be a habit.

00:23:25.130 --> 00:23:26.090
You run the Blue Dahlia.

00:23:26.410 --> 00:23:27.530
I'll take care of my private life.

00:23:28.410 --> 00:23:29.430
We're hooked up together, Eddie.

00:23:30.600 --> 00:23:32.600
You gettin' a jam, I gettin' a jam.

00:23:35.210 --> 00:23:36.370
You can forget Helen Morrison.

00:23:38.380 --> 00:23:39.780
Her husband's back from the South Pacific.

00:23:40.210 --> 00:23:40.970
Let him take care of her.

00:23:49.830 --> 00:23:51.590
You think my wife left me because of another woman?

00:23:53.260 --> 00:23:54.480
It was something else entirely, Leo.

00:23:55.370 --> 00:23:57.200
Like how you make some of your dough?

00:23:58.060 --> 00:23:59.520
Like you're putting in with people like me?

00:24:01.380 --> 00:24:06.340
She was in the bar a little while ago. Just left.

00:24:07.620 --> 00:24:10.750
Gave me a message for you. Going out of town for a few days.

00:24:12.020 --> 00:24:13.180
Saved some money on flowers.

00:24:13.520 --> 00:24:14.890
Could have told me that.

00:24:15.000 --> 00:24:18.500
Maybe she figured it'd sound worse coming from me.

00:24:18.620 --> 00:24:22.710
Any checks for me to sign?

00:24:22.850 --> 00:24:23.770
Yeah, there's a few.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:31.420
Ever know a guy named Quinlan?

00:24:31.690 --> 00:24:34.280
Never heard of him.

00:24:34.340 --> 00:24:36.230
Just stretched somewhere back east.

00:24:36.290 --> 00:24:38.610
Not interested, huh?

00:24:40.050 --> 00:24:40.390
Okay.

00:24:42.140 --> 00:24:43.320
Don't get cute with me, Leo.

00:24:43.440 --> 00:24:44.980
Nothing cute about it.

00:24:46.530 --> 00:24:49.030
I heard this criminal spoke to you in the parking lot the other night,

00:24:49.330 --> 00:24:50.870
when you were with Mrs. Morrison.

00:24:51.110 --> 00:24:53.380
Called you by some other name.

00:24:53.500 --> 00:24:56.030
Did he?

00:24:56.070 --> 00:24:57.530
If you say he didn't.

00:24:57.780 --> 00:24:58.780
But it doesn't matter now anyway.

00:25:00.060 --> 00:25:02.900
Wyndham was moped off a few nights ago over on East 5th.

00:25:04.720 --> 00:25:05.780
I'll make sure you think I'd be interested.

00:25:05.980 --> 00:25:09.240
Just don't get too complicated, Eddie.

00:25:09.380 --> 00:25:12.550
When a man gets too complicated, he's unhappy.

00:25:12.870 --> 00:25:14.930
And when he's unhappy...

00:25:16.790 --> 00:25:17.270
runs out.

00:25:31.850 --> 00:25:39.910
Oh, baby, I was just gonna call you.

00:25:40.460 --> 00:25:42.760
Well, it's about time. I've been calling you all evening.

00:25:45.800 --> 00:25:46.480
Hold on a minute.

00:26:00.508 --> 00:26:01.008
Hello?

00:26:03.612 --> 00:26:05.612
Of course he's not here.

00:26:06.012 --> 00:26:07.852
No, he hasn't just stepped out.

00:26:08.380 --> 00:26:09.040
He's gone.

00:26:09.756 --> 00:26:11.996
G-O-N-E. Gone.

00:26:12.412 --> 00:26:13.492
You'll be back, all right, baby.

00:26:14.268 --> 00:26:15.208
It's all my fault.

00:26:17.980 --> 00:26:19.020
I think he's a nice guy.

00:26:21.212 --> 00:26:22.092
He was so far away.

00:26:22.780 --> 00:26:23.660
I'd never seen him.

00:26:24.796 --> 00:26:26.016
I guess I didn't realize how it looked.

00:26:31.052 --> 00:26:31.632
Now, wait a minute.

00:26:32.012 --> 00:26:33.812
I'm not hinting, I'm saying it straight out.

00:26:34.828 --> 00:26:36.068
I think we better call it a day.

00:26:36.812 --> 00:26:38.572
Supposing I don't want to call it a day.

00:26:39.372 --> 00:26:41.932
Two walkouts in one evening would be just a little too much for me.

00:26:42.012 --> 00:26:42.712
Eddie, ever think of that?

00:26:43.788 --> 00:26:47.008
And if I don't want to call it a day, I'm quite sure you won't.

00:26:47.660 --> 00:26:49.020
for a very good reason.

00:26:50.028 --> 00:26:51.148
I better come over and talk to you, huh?

00:26:56.268 --> 00:26:56.828
Say half an hour?

00:27:03.164 --> 00:27:04.604
I told you she was poison.

00:27:05.404 --> 00:27:06.964
They're all poisoned sooner or later.

00:27:09.596 --> 00:27:10.336
Almost all.

00:27:11.164 --> 00:27:11.464
Anyway.

00:27:32.492 --> 00:27:33.012
Get in.

00:27:40.524 --> 00:27:42.744
Well, you could get wetter if you lay down on the gutter.

00:27:54.284 --> 00:27:55.264
I wasn't trying to get wet.

00:28:02.490 --> 00:28:05.050
You ought to have more sense than to take chances with strangers like this.

00:28:06.480 --> 00:28:09.520
Funny, but practically all the people I know were strangers when I met them.

00:28:11.240 --> 00:28:12.940
I'm going to Malibu. Is that any use to you?

00:28:14.290 --> 00:28:15.090
What's in Malibu?

00:28:15.840 --> 00:28:18.300
Houses, people. I have some friends there.

00:28:19.520 --> 00:28:20.080
Any hotels?

00:28:21.900 --> 00:28:22.540
Motel, maybe.

00:28:25.720 --> 00:28:27.200
Pick up many people like this at night?

00:28:29.780 --> 00:28:29.940
Not...

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:35.370
Not many. Only one or two at a time. You're right.

00:28:36.730 --> 00:28:36.990
Right?

00:28:37.530 --> 00:28:38.470
That wasn't funny.

00:28:41.650 --> 00:28:43.570
Sorry, but nothing's very funny to me tonight.

00:28:47.120 --> 00:28:49.220
It all blows up in your face sometimes, doesn't it?

00:28:51.400 --> 00:28:51.760
What does?

00:28:52.310 --> 00:28:54.200
Whatever you're doing. Wherever you're going.

00:28:56.080 --> 00:28:57.220
I thought you were going to Malibu.

00:28:57.320 --> 00:28:58.980
I flipped a coin.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:00.760
I got a Malibu.

00:29:00.840 --> 00:29:01.860
Tails, I got a Laguna.

00:29:03.050 --> 00:29:04.950
What happens if the coin rolls into the Davenport?

00:29:05.200 --> 00:29:06.140
You got a long picture.

00:29:08.490 --> 00:29:09.810
Oh, you can smile.

00:29:10.030 --> 00:29:10.970
I was beginning to wonder.

00:29:40.430 --> 00:29:41.090
Sure you won't have one?

00:29:41.310 --> 00:29:41.910
No, thanks.

00:29:55.980 --> 00:29:56.520
Bag in your way?

00:29:57.290 --> 00:29:57.590
No.

00:29:57.960 --> 00:29:59.940
I was just wondering what the JM stood for.

00:30:01.500 --> 00:30:02.640
You don't have to wonder, I'll tell you.

00:30:03.160 --> 00:30:05.520
That's no fun. Let me see.

00:30:06.280 --> 00:30:07.280
How about Jack Mason?

00:30:10.020 --> 00:30:11.460
It's fine for somebody named Jack Mason.

00:30:12.940 --> 00:30:16.180
Well, then, how about Jeremiah McGonagall?

00:30:17.600 --> 00:30:19.420
Nobody was ever named Jeremiah McGonagall.

00:30:20.390 --> 00:30:22.940
Fine. I think I like Jeremiah McGonagall.

00:30:24.050 --> 00:30:25.620
Dull. No sense of humor.

00:30:26.520 --> 00:30:27.900
Well, that's two strikes on me.

00:30:30.320 --> 00:30:31.040
How about Jimmy Moore?

00:30:31.980 --> 00:30:34.740
Jimmy Moore? Is that really your name?

00:30:36.130 --> 00:30:36.730
Don't you like it?

00:30:37.970 --> 00:30:39.610
I once knew a boy by the name of Jimmy.

00:30:40.170 --> 00:30:41.190
He had rabbit teeth.

00:30:42.210 --> 00:30:43.430
I guess I'll learn to forget him, though.

00:30:43.510 --> 00:30:44.550
I was only eight years old.

00:30:44.730 --> 00:30:54.820
You sure that corn you flipped came up heads?

00:30:55.530 --> 00:30:56.090
Yes, why?

00:30:57.980 --> 00:30:59.000
Malibu, we just passed.

00:31:04.960 --> 00:31:10.630
Where have you been? Out where?

00:31:14.520 --> 00:31:15.260
Guess I got lost.

00:31:15.610 --> 00:31:16.390
You guessed, don't you know?

00:31:18.850 --> 00:31:22.460
Yeah, I got lost. Where's Johnny?

00:31:23.380 --> 00:31:24.280
Johnny hasn't been here.

00:31:28.480 --> 00:31:29.240
Buzzer, are you all right?

00:31:30.280 --> 00:31:32.000
Certainly I'm all right. Why wouldn't I be all right?

00:31:33.520 --> 00:31:35.220
What's the idea of running out without telling me?

00:31:35.340 --> 00:31:36.560
You've been gone a couple of hours.

00:31:44.410 --> 00:31:46.270
Well, for Pete's sake, you might at least say something.

00:31:47.680 --> 00:31:48.580
I'm sleepy, George.

00:32:18.080 --> 00:32:20.760
I'd better telephone my friends and they'll think something's happened.

00:32:21.000 --> 00:32:21.800
It won't be long.

00:32:38.990 --> 00:32:45.100
Jenny! The idea.

00:32:45.830 --> 00:32:46.650
It's the end of the line.

00:32:47.480 --> 00:32:47.920
Is it?

00:32:48.610 --> 00:32:51.290
It has to be. It's a long way back to Malibu.

00:32:52.230 --> 00:32:53.070
Well, what about you?

00:32:53.960 --> 00:32:59.010
I'll make up. And if I knew how, this is where I'd say thanks for everything.

00:33:00.250 --> 00:33:01.530
I didn't do it for thanks.

00:33:03.200 --> 00:33:03.760
I know that.

00:33:05.350 --> 00:33:06.850
Well, don't you even say goodnight?

00:33:09.570 --> 00:33:09.870
Bye.

00:33:10.750 --> 00:33:11.730
And it's tough to say goodbye.

00:33:14.860 --> 00:33:15.460
Why is it?

00:33:15.950 --> 00:33:17.450
You've never seen me before tonight.

00:33:19.210 --> 00:33:20.390
Every guy's seen you before.

00:33:20.940 --> 00:33:21.300
Somewhere.

00:33:22.820 --> 00:33:23.740
The trick is to find you.

00:33:30.700 --> 00:33:34.160
And now, folks, bright and early on this beautiful sunny day,

00:33:34.380 --> 00:33:38.020
the flowers are fresh from the rain, and there isn't a cloud in the sky.

00:33:38.360 --> 00:33:40.840
We bring you once again your favorite breakfast program,

00:33:41.360 --> 00:33:42.560
Melodies of the Morning.

00:33:45.730 --> 00:33:47.030
Well, well, well.

00:33:48.080 --> 00:33:49.100
Andre again.

00:33:51.680 --> 00:33:53.000
Couldn't make it to bed, huh?

00:33:54.460 --> 00:33:56.690
Honey, I don't know where you put it.

00:33:59.460 --> 00:33:59.960
Come on, now.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:28.120
Let's oh, what's that? I'll be right over and call mr. Hughes over there

00:34:31.790 --> 00:34:33.260
Out. And keep your mouth shut.

00:34:33.850 --> 00:34:34.750
Ever know me not to?

00:34:35.720 --> 00:34:37.080
Looks like there was a brawl here.

00:34:37.600 --> 00:34:41.550
Yeah. Been dead for hours.

00:34:41.870 --> 00:34:42.190
Suicide?

00:34:43.270 --> 00:34:43.750
Could be.

00:34:43.930 --> 00:34:44.310
Better be.

00:34:45.690 --> 00:34:47.460
Uh-uh. Too much gun.

00:34:47.600 --> 00:34:49.340
Now, don't start playing detective, Dad.

00:34:49.460 --> 00:34:51.020
We'll have enough of that from the professionals.

00:34:51.300 --> 00:34:52.100
What's the number down there?

00:34:52.240 --> 00:34:54.420
Well, don't you think we ought to look around a bit before we call the police?

00:34:54.660 --> 00:34:55.180
Don't be a fool.

00:34:55.380 --> 00:34:57.340
The sooner we get started, the sooner we get her out of here.

00:34:57.420 --> 00:34:57.920
What's the number?

00:34:58.230 --> 00:34:59.450
Michigan 5211.

00:35:01.210 --> 00:35:01.730
Good morning.

00:35:01.930 --> 00:35:02.090
Good morning.

00:35:03.790 --> 00:35:05.490
I'll continue with our morning music.

00:35:11.450 --> 00:35:11.890
Elena?

00:35:17.700 --> 00:35:18.920
Take the number three with orange juice.

00:35:52.490 --> 00:35:52.710
with me.

00:36:00.830 --> 00:36:02.050
I guess it's where we left it.

00:36:02.460 --> 00:36:03.660
I stayed here at the inn.

00:36:04.880 --> 00:36:05.180
Why?

00:36:06.420 --> 00:36:07.540
Do I have to have a reason?

00:36:09.080 --> 00:36:09.240
No.

00:36:16.700 --> 00:36:17.980
Nice after the rain, isn't it?

00:36:18.850 --> 00:36:18.990
Uh-huh.

00:36:25.590 --> 00:36:26.690
Didn't expect to see you again.

00:36:29.250 --> 00:36:29.970
Jimmy, why don't you go?

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:31.720
Go back and fix it up before it's too late.

00:36:34.920 --> 00:36:37.040
Maybe you'd like it better if I'd mind my own business.

00:36:38.520 --> 00:36:39.100
You think you could?

00:36:40.190 --> 00:36:40.910
I could try.

00:36:42.270 --> 00:36:42.830
My wife.

00:36:46.270 --> 00:36:47.310
Had an idea it might be.

00:36:48.180 --> 00:36:49.200
There's nothing to fix up.

00:36:50.080 --> 00:36:51.960
And if there was, I wouldn't want to fix it up anyway.

00:36:52.160 --> 00:36:59.980
What about you, who aren't going to Malibu?

00:37:00.060 --> 00:37:05.540
You were trying to run out in your cell, like me.

00:37:07.830 --> 00:37:08.470
Maybe you're right.

00:37:12.480 --> 00:37:14.390
Well, where do we go from here?

00:37:14.610 --> 00:37:26.540
We'll go anywhere.

00:37:28.360 --> 00:37:29.400
We said goodbye last night.

00:37:30.960 --> 00:37:34.430
You catch the bus for up north and I go back to Malibu.

00:37:37.780 --> 00:37:38.160
That's right.

00:37:47.070 --> 00:37:50.990
Could we take a walk along the beach first and look for moonstones?

00:37:52.270 --> 00:37:52.790
Tide's out.

00:37:57.280 --> 00:37:58.400
You can go waiting, if you like.

00:38:00.570 --> 00:38:03.430
If I run upstairs and change my shoes, will you be here when I get back?

00:38:04.440 --> 00:38:04.640
Aye.

00:38:05.680 --> 00:38:06.540
Not like last night?

00:38:07.980 --> 00:38:08.260
No.

00:38:16.110 --> 00:38:16.830
Check, please.

00:38:17.550 --> 00:38:17.870
Yes, sir.

00:38:18.410 --> 00:38:21.330
The cause of a death has so far not been definitely established.

00:38:21.970 --> 00:38:26.130
All it's sought for questioning is her husband, Lieutenant Commander John Morrison,

00:38:26.670 --> 00:38:28.670
recently returned from the South Pacific.

00:38:29.490 --> 00:38:29.970
Lieutenant...

00:38:30.030 --> 00:38:39.720
Commander Morrison is described as about 28 years old, weight 160 pounds, light brown hair, light brown or blue eyes.

00:38:40.760 --> 00:38:46.560
When last seen, he was wearing civilian clothes with a navy raincoat and was carrying a civilian suitcase.

00:38:47.520 --> 00:38:53.160
Her lifeless body was found sprawled down at Davenport in her exclusive Wilshire Boulevard hotel bungalow.

00:38:53.200 --> 00:38:56.880
Passengers for bus 382, leaving for Los Angeles. All aboard.

00:38:57.100 --> 00:38:59.980
The discovery occurred early this morning when neighbors complained...

00:39:00.090 --> 00:39:01.670
about the loud playing of the radio.

00:39:02.530 --> 00:39:04.150
The cause of her death has so far

00:39:04.150 --> 00:39:05.670
not been definitely established.

00:39:14.710 --> 00:39:15.150
That's mine.

00:39:15.330 --> 00:39:16.110
Oh, I'm a hearty.

00:39:16.700 --> 00:39:17.120
Wait a minute.

00:39:17.540 --> 00:39:18.920
Okay, okay, let's measure it.

00:39:19.190 --> 00:39:19.370
All right.

00:39:22.900 --> 00:39:23.560
Anything for us?

00:39:23.880 --> 00:39:27.480
No, get your junk off this bench.

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:30.400
Why are you here?

00:39:32.820 --> 00:39:34.260
How do you like being pinched, George?

00:39:34.720 --> 00:39:35.680
We're not pinched, relax.

00:39:36.380 --> 00:39:36.860
What's the difference?

00:39:36.960 --> 00:39:38.320
They brought us here and we're here.

00:39:43.020 --> 00:39:43.900
What's your name, Copper?

00:39:44.480 --> 00:39:44.960
Save it.

00:39:47.560 --> 00:39:48.560
Maybe they don't have names.

00:39:48.720 --> 00:39:49.760
Maybe they just have numbers.

00:39:50.140 --> 00:39:51.120
Calm down, can't you?

00:39:51.280 --> 00:39:56.560
How long do we have to wait here, Copper?

00:39:58.020 --> 00:39:59.660
Until the captain gets ready for you.

00:40:00.060 --> 00:40:01.500
And don't call me copper.

00:40:02.270 --> 00:40:04.090
You get that, George? He says don't call him copper.

00:40:04.340 --> 00:40:11.990
Is it all right if we smoke two copper?

00:40:15.950 --> 00:40:16.850
You want to make trouble?

00:40:17.130 --> 00:40:26.400
Yeah, you want some, George?

00:40:30.160 --> 00:40:31.380
Thanks, copper.

00:40:35.070 --> 00:40:35.790
Hendrickson's office, please.

00:40:36.460 --> 00:40:37.840
Right there. Get this guy here.

00:40:37.920 --> 00:40:38.300
Who is he?

00:40:38.380 --> 00:40:38.860
Eddie Harwood.

00:40:38.920 --> 00:40:40.730
Hold it, Mr. Harwood.

00:40:40.830 --> 00:40:42.210
Nothing doing, fellas. Skip it.

00:40:45.450 --> 00:40:47.120
Hendrickson, please. I'm Eddie Harwood.

00:40:47.910 --> 00:40:48.630
Just have a seat.

00:40:50.280 --> 00:40:51.100
Hello, Mr. Harwood.

00:40:51.260 --> 00:40:55.060
Hello, Dad.

00:40:57.600 --> 00:40:58.280
Harwood's here, too.

00:41:06.400 --> 00:41:07.340
Push the buzzer, will you, Cap?

00:41:10.160 --> 00:41:12.620
Captain Hendrickson's office, Homicide Bureau.

00:41:13.440 --> 00:41:14.820
Detective Lieutenant Lloyd speaking.

00:41:15.640 --> 00:41:16.360
Call back, please.

00:41:20.330 --> 00:41:20.550
Shoot.

00:41:28.330 --> 00:41:28.490
Okay.

00:41:29.070 --> 00:41:29.490
Stand by.

00:41:30.410 --> 00:41:32.730
What do you want first, Cap?

00:41:33.290 --> 00:41:35.900
Oh, let's take Harwood. Pity to keep him waiting.

00:41:36.080 --> 00:41:39.060
Right. Come in, Mr. Harwood.

00:41:39.200 --> 00:41:47.970
I won't take up much of your time, Mr. Harwood,

00:41:48.050 --> 00:41:50.980
but I always like to meet the people involved in the investigation.

00:41:52.120 --> 00:41:52.700
Involved how?

00:41:54.600 --> 00:41:59.960
Sit down. You knew Mrs. Morris...

00:42:02.080 --> 00:42:02.620
Fairly well.

00:42:02.760 --> 00:42:04.880
How long have you known her?

00:42:06.990 --> 00:42:07.650
You've got all that.

00:42:08.740 --> 00:42:09.280
So I have.

00:42:09.540 --> 00:42:10.680
Slightly less than a year.

00:42:11.750 --> 00:42:12.950
Met her through mutual friends.

00:42:13.280 --> 00:42:13.580
Correct.

00:42:15.350 --> 00:42:16.870
She owned a business in Beverly Hills.

00:42:17.150 --> 00:42:18.130
Do you have any interest in that?

00:42:18.890 --> 00:42:20.430
I loaned her some money when she first bought it.

00:42:20.530 --> 00:42:21.230
The money's been repaid.

00:42:21.790 --> 00:42:24.090
I see. Purely a business transaction.

00:42:26.180 --> 00:42:28.800
I'd regard a secured loan at 6% as a business transaction.

00:42:29.300 --> 00:42:29.980
You suppose you think I'm...

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:35.660
wasting your time. You're married, aren't you, Mr. Harwood? My wife and I are separated. You want to

00:42:35.660 --> 00:42:42.010
know why? Not unless it has a bearing on your relations with Mrs. Morrison. It hasn't. Where

00:42:42.010 --> 00:42:53.370
is Mrs. Harwood at the moment? No idea. Any idea where she was last night? No. Look here,

00:42:53.450 --> 00:42:56.310
Hendrickson, if you think my wife had anything to do with Helen Morrison's murder,

00:43:01.980 --> 00:43:04.820
So you're taking it for granted that Mrs. Morrison was murdered, are you?

00:43:06.460 --> 00:43:07.160
Well, wasn't she?

00:43:07.940 --> 00:43:09.600
We haven't called it murder so far.

00:43:10.410 --> 00:43:18.000
Yes, but the newspapers... Well, then I just assumed it.

00:43:19.250 --> 00:43:22.750
Sure, but you're quite right. She was murdered.

00:43:23.260 --> 00:43:27.270
We have the autopsy report now. Nitrate tests of her hands.

00:43:29.180 --> 00:43:29.580
Well...

00:43:30.860 --> 00:43:44.590
for coming in mr harwood i guess that's all for now am i under suspicion i don't know how do you feel

00:43:44.590 --> 00:43:45.010
about it

00:44:04.060 --> 00:44:16.540
Hello, George. Isn't George there? George Copeland.

00:44:17.200 --> 00:44:19.340
No, George isn't here right now. Who's just calling?

00:44:20.930 --> 00:44:21.890
Who's calling, I said?

00:44:35.240 --> 00:44:37.800
There's just one thing I'd like you gentlemen to bear in mind.

00:44:38.540 --> 00:44:43.300
Even if you are close friends of Morrison's, you can't help him to hide out, so don't try.

00:44:44.290 --> 00:44:46.460
I'm an attorney, Captain. I understand perfectly.

00:44:47.530 --> 00:44:51.600
I'm glad to hear it. If he gets in touch with you, make him come in.

00:44:51.880 --> 00:44:53.700
It's the only sensible thing for him to do.

00:44:54.200 --> 00:44:59.280
Baloney! If you think we're going to help you tie a murder to a guy who's flown us through 112 missions,

00:44:59.380 --> 00:44:59.980
you're off your n...

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:03.600
We haven't accused Morrison of murder so far.

00:45:03.740 --> 00:45:04.880
No, what's holding you up?

00:45:13.240 --> 00:45:15.080
Have these men driven back to their apartment.

00:45:16.740 --> 00:45:17.580
Bring in that new old.

00:45:25.400 --> 00:45:26.340
Any chance for a room here?

00:45:26.750 --> 00:45:29.410
I'm sorry, sir. We have not a vacancy in eight weeks.

00:45:30.510 --> 00:45:31.490
Do you know where I can find one?

00:45:31.670 --> 00:45:33.610
That's a pretty difficult thing to say these days.

00:45:34.130 --> 00:45:35.430
I'm afraid I can't help you.

00:45:36.960 --> 00:45:37.520
All right, thanks.

00:45:46.830 --> 00:45:49.000
You, just a minute.

00:45:55.670 --> 00:45:56.190
Got a match?

00:45:58.070 --> 00:45:58.430
Okay.

00:45:59.440 --> 00:45:59.980
Here's one of my...

00:46:01.520 --> 00:46:02.860
Suitcase gets kind of heavy, don't it?

00:46:03.920 --> 00:46:04.700
Yeah, what's to you?

00:46:06.110 --> 00:46:07.550
Every hotel in town's loaded.

00:46:07.800 --> 00:46:09.020
Thought it might be a little pelt.

00:46:09.450 --> 00:46:11.290
Little place down on Santa Monica Boulevard.

00:46:12.800 --> 00:46:13.320
What's the racket?

00:46:13.940 --> 00:46:15.260
Think it's a racket? Call a cop.

00:46:19.190 --> 00:46:20.150
How far away is this place?

00:46:20.450 --> 00:46:28.520
About six blocks. Transportation and everything.

00:46:29.490 --> 00:46:29.850
Okay.

00:46:32.780 --> 00:46:41.600
Okay. You saw Harwood go up to this dame's apartment and knock on the door. No answer.

00:46:42.080 --> 00:46:47.340
You went away. Went away where? Well, you see, Captain, there's a side gate to the hotel grounds.

00:46:47.440 --> 00:46:50.780
We've seen the joint. Well, that's where he went out. What time was this?

00:46:51.320 --> 00:46:56.510
Well, I've told you, gentlemen. Tell us again. It was about seven o'clock. It was raining.

00:46:56.770 --> 00:46:59.670
You like standing in the rain? I gotta make my rounds.

00:47:00.000 --> 00:47:02.040
Everything's okay. Nobody cutting up too much.

00:47:02.140 --> 00:47:03.620
You got a passkey to the bungalows?

00:47:05.260 --> 00:47:06.320
Surely you don't think I...

00:47:06.320 --> 00:47:10.470
Why not? Plenty of genial old parties like you commit murders.

00:47:11.280 --> 00:47:12.900
That isn't a very nice thing to say, Captain.

00:47:14.300 --> 00:47:16.620
Mrs. Morrison's lights were on. The radio was going.

00:47:16.740 --> 00:47:17.640
Why would I want to get in?

00:47:17.760 --> 00:47:18.640
You tell us.

00:47:18.820 --> 00:47:20.540
She didn't answer when Harwood knocked.

00:47:20.890 --> 00:47:21.610
Didn't that interest you?

00:47:21.850 --> 00:47:23.150
Would that be any of my business?

00:47:23.410 --> 00:47:29.600
You boys got a nice technique.

00:47:31.340 --> 00:47:35.970
Had me worried for a minute. No hard feelings, of course.

00:47:37.770 --> 00:47:39.500
That's all, Newell, for now.

00:47:42.140 --> 00:47:43.440
It was a terrible thing for the hotel.

00:47:43.640 --> 00:47:46.560
Kind of tough on the Morrison Dame, too. Go on, beat it.

00:48:01.530 --> 00:48:02.210
Let's dump the hotel.

00:48:02.410 --> 00:48:03.710
That's what the sign said.

00:48:03.870 --> 00:48:06.280
Clean sheets every day, they tell me.

00:48:06.380 --> 00:48:09.480
How often do they change the fleas?

00:48:10.010 --> 00:48:10.770
Very funny.

00:48:15.350 --> 00:48:22.790
customer, Carelli. That'll be ten bucks.

00:48:35.116 --> 00:48:36.116
in advance.

00:48:36.268 --> 00:48:36.908
Mr. Moore?

00:48:47.436 --> 00:48:48.456
There'll be ten for us, too.

00:48:49.036 --> 00:48:49.256
What?

00:48:50.028 --> 00:48:50.788
Our, uh...

00:48:50.796 --> 00:48:51.616
Commission, get it?

00:48:54.188 --> 00:48:54.748
Give me back that money.

00:48:56.332 --> 00:48:57.952
You ain't gonna get difficult, are you, pal?

00:49:01.760 --> 00:49:02.840
Okay, boys, you win.

00:49:04.650 --> 00:49:22.230
Hot, ain't it?

00:49:23.050 --> 00:49:23.250
Yeah.

00:49:25.360 --> 00:49:25.840
Hi, Corelli.

00:49:29.140 --> 00:49:29.800
Anybody up here?

00:49:30.940 --> 00:49:31.440
Why?

00:49:32.350 --> 00:49:35.760
Some crazy woman driver just tore a fender off it.

00:49:36.410 --> 00:49:37.250
I didn't hear nothing.

00:49:38.610 --> 00:49:38.930
No?

00:49:39.050 --> 00:49:40.520
What's a fender?

00:49:40.680 --> 00:49:41.280
Forget it.

00:49:41.380 --> 00:49:44.760
Your car?

00:49:45.860 --> 00:49:46.120
Could be.

00:49:46.240 --> 00:49:48.690
Come on down, then. We gotta make a report.

00:49:49.850 --> 00:49:50.610
Let's skip it, huh?

00:49:50.830 --> 00:49:53.050
You heard what I said, didn't you?

00:49:53.110 --> 00:49:54.310
Come on down. That's a hot car.

00:49:54.610 --> 00:49:59.120
Come on, get back here.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:05.520
Come on, get up, you. Come on, quick. Turn around. That's it.

00:50:05.720 --> 00:50:09.340
You want to play rough, huh? You boys make it easy for us.

00:50:09.460 --> 00:50:11.330
Get going.

00:50:15.410 --> 00:50:15.730
Who are you?

00:50:17.180 --> 00:50:18.540
Jimmy Moore, San Francisco.

00:50:18.740 --> 00:50:20.120
All right, Corrales?

00:50:20.240 --> 00:50:21.960
Yeah, he just registered.

00:50:23.490 --> 00:50:23.890
Okay.

00:50:24.110 --> 00:50:25.560
Get moving.

00:50:25.740 --> 00:50:28.260
Thanks, pal.

00:50:35.116 --> 00:50:36.156
You still want that room?

00:50:37.676 --> 00:50:38.876
You're sure nobody's dead, isn't it?

00:50:41.836 --> 00:50:42.736
Right back this way.

00:50:45.676 --> 00:50:47.296
You live in San Francisco, Mr. Moore?

00:50:48.684 --> 00:50:49.684
Yeah, when I'm there.

00:50:50.412 --> 00:50:51.072
Nice town.

00:50:54.188 --> 00:50:55.168
I like it here better.

00:51:01.052 --> 00:51:02.772
Anything you need, just ask for it.

00:51:04.124 --> 00:51:04.704
Where's your phone?

00:51:05.308 --> 00:51:06.068
back down the hole.

00:51:44.588 --> 00:51:44.848
Howard.

00:52:33.230 --> 00:52:33.790
We'll let you in.

00:52:35.770 --> 00:52:37.830
House man. Don't have much trouble getting into places.

00:52:38.780 --> 00:52:40.300
I come up the forest stairs.

00:52:41.790 --> 00:52:43.450
Thought it was a good idea not to be seen.

00:52:46.050 --> 00:52:46.310
Drink?

00:52:47.580 --> 00:52:48.420
Don't mind if I do.

00:52:49.820 --> 00:52:50.780
Easy on the water.

00:52:53.920 --> 00:52:56.640
I told the homicide boys a good straight story.

00:52:57.580 --> 00:52:58.460
They're satisfied.

00:52:59.540 --> 00:52:59.960
But a day...

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:06.730
anyway but you know how these sticks are tomorrow they might get to figure and i was holding

00:53:06.730 --> 00:53:22.470
something back this you're holding something back well i uh hung around a while after you

00:53:22.470 --> 00:53:29.910
knocked on mrs morrison's door i mean pretty wet wasn't it weather don't bother me used to be a cop

00:53:30.030 --> 00:53:51.180
myself 15 years of it sit down how much they pay you over there 28 a week and found not very much

00:53:51.180 --> 00:53:54.240
is it it's not for a fact well thanks

00:54:00.250 --> 00:54:02.670
So you thought you'd like to make a little more, and that's why you're here, huh?

00:54:03.400 --> 00:54:05.360
Oh, you got me all wrong, Mr. Harwood.

00:54:05.420 --> 00:54:06.560
Yeah, I know, I know.

00:54:09.880 --> 00:54:10.560
How old are you, Dad?

00:54:11.920 --> 00:54:12.680
Going on 57.

00:54:13.620 --> 00:54:16.120
Well, you've got a lot of life left, unless you get careless.

00:54:17.170 --> 00:54:18.510
I don't aim to get careless.

00:54:20.460 --> 00:54:21.920
Cops don't pay you any money, and I do.

00:54:26.960 --> 00:54:29.960
Gee, this sure is white of you, Harwood.

00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:32.750
Yes, isn't it? Finished your drink?

00:54:44.500 --> 00:54:45.500
I guess I'd better be going now.

00:54:46.220 --> 00:54:53.780
Wait a minute, forgot your cigar. I think it's out.

00:54:58.060 --> 00:54:59.560
Cigars go out awful easy, don't they, Dad?

00:55:05.760 --> 00:55:25.200
Good night. Hello, Eddie. Hello, baby.

00:55:26.000 --> 00:55:29.690
Long time, no see. Not so long, is it?

00:55:32.880 --> 00:55:35.300
You even send these blue flowers to yourself, don't you?

00:55:35.950 --> 00:55:36.910
I thought you went out of town.

00:55:38.200 --> 00:55:38.900
I came back.

00:55:44.380 --> 00:55:45.580
You still have this around.

00:55:47.260 --> 00:55:47.900
Sentimentalist, aren't you?

00:55:48.750 --> 00:55:49.810
I only wish I had you with it.

00:55:50.830 --> 00:55:52.010
Sure, I know I've got lots of faults,

00:55:52.150 --> 00:55:54.590
but being in love with you isn't one of them, is it?

00:55:56.220 --> 00:55:56.740
Look, baby.

00:55:58.890 --> 00:55:59.490
It's too late, Eddie.

00:56:01.660 --> 00:56:04.160
Why? Why is it too late?

00:56:05.420 --> 00:56:06.000
Just is.

00:56:09.130 --> 00:56:11.470
Helen Morrison didn't mean anything to me alive.

00:56:11.890 --> 00:56:12.190
No.

00:56:15.660 --> 00:56:17.040
She doesn't mean anything to me dead.

00:56:18.520 --> 00:56:19.960
She means something to the police, though.

00:56:20.740 --> 00:56:23.660
The police have the whole story, my part of it, in any case.

00:56:24.550 --> 00:56:25.310
How do they like it?

00:56:26.480 --> 00:56:27.660
As well as they ever like anything.

00:56:31.440 --> 00:56:33.460
Well, I guess everything's lovely then.

00:56:39.090 --> 00:56:39.830
Who did kill her, Eddie?

00:56:42.230 --> 00:56:42.870
Did you read the papers?

00:56:43.810 --> 00:56:45.530
I don't have to believe everything I see in them.

00:56:46.340 --> 00:56:48.520
Well, if Morrison didn't kill her, he certainly set himself up pretty.

00:56:49.460 --> 00:56:50.680
He couldn't even have his initials on it.

00:56:51.470 --> 00:56:52.030
Careless of him.

00:56:52.600 --> 00:56:53.040
I met him.

00:56:53.500 --> 00:56:54.980
He's the kind of guy who wouldn't care much what he did.

00:56:55.800 --> 00:56:57.160
When he walked in on that party, he...

00:56:57.160 --> 00:56:57.800
He didn't like it.

00:57:01.280 --> 00:57:01.800
How would you know?

00:57:03.050 --> 00:57:04.630
I know the kind of party it would be.

00:57:05.940 --> 00:57:07.600
Well, so long as I know you're all right, Eddie.

00:57:08.940 --> 00:57:10.160
So I do mean that much to you?

00:57:11.190 --> 00:57:11.830
I guess so.

00:57:44.650 --> 00:57:45.870
Take me to the mezzanine, please.

00:57:47.220 --> 00:57:48.790
Yes, sir. Is Mr. Harwood in?

00:57:48.890 --> 00:57:51.170
I'll see. Name, please.

00:57:52.100 --> 00:57:55.060
Moore. Mr. Harwood?

00:58:00.860 --> 00:58:01.840
Give me the desk, please.

00:58:03.120 --> 00:58:04.600
Mr. Harwood's line is busy at the moment.

00:58:05.700 --> 00:58:06.440
What's his apartment number?

00:58:06.620 --> 00:58:07.900
Oh, I'm sorry. You'll have to be announced.

00:58:08.400 --> 00:58:09.200
I'll try again in a moment.

00:58:13.350 --> 00:58:13.670
Desk?

00:58:15.280 --> 00:58:15.500
Who?

00:58:16.900 --> 00:58:17.400
Just a minute.

00:58:19.010 --> 00:58:19.410
You, sir.

00:58:21.460 --> 00:58:21.720
Me?

00:58:27.520 --> 00:58:29.820
Please don't ask any questions.

00:58:30.000 --> 00:58:35.060
get out of the hotel right away yeah but why does it take so long because when a man's in the service

00:58:35.060 --> 00:58:40.590
they file his folder in Washington they have to get it from there what I'm wondering is who glommed

00:58:40.590 --> 00:58:45.930
the photo the maid said was in the bedroom my name was Morrison it'd be me yeah the description

00:58:45.930 --> 00:58:59.980
we got could fit a thousand guys Harwood please Captain Hendrickson calling yes sir

00:59:04.030 --> 00:59:04.570
Mr. Harwood.

00:59:32.040 --> 00:59:32.820
I don't think so.

00:59:34.460 --> 00:59:34.960
It's too bad.

00:59:36.170 --> 00:59:37.050
Do you want to get caught?

00:59:38.460 --> 00:59:40.380
When did you find out that somebody was trying to catch me?

00:59:41.630 --> 00:59:43.430
This morning, when I saw you get rid of your coat.

00:59:43.590 --> 00:59:48.760
You angry at me for trying to help you, Jimmy?

00:59:50.120 --> 00:59:51.760
Maybe you'd better call me by my right name.

00:59:53.080 --> 00:59:54.780
None of this would make any sense if you didn't know it.

00:59:56.570 --> 00:59:57.890
All right, Johnny.

00:59:59.670 --> 00:59:59.970
Johnny's...

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:15.220
quite a nice name too. Jimmy didn't have the police after him. Takes a lot of lights to make

01:00:15.220 --> 01:00:28.600
a city, doesn't it? I know you didn't kill your wife, Johnny. You do? How? Just from knowing you.

01:00:30.540 --> 01:00:31.400
You don't know me that well.

01:00:32.250 --> 01:00:32.830
Well enough.

01:00:34.280 --> 01:00:36.380
You think you have to find out who did kill her, though, don't you?

01:00:38.220 --> 01:00:39.000
Something like that.

01:00:45.070 --> 01:00:46.950
You wonder why I don't let the police do that job.

01:00:47.980 --> 01:00:49.460
Have I acted as if I thought that?

01:00:50.530 --> 01:00:51.390
They're looking for me.

01:00:53.120 --> 01:00:55.880
And if they catch me, they're not going to worry about trying to pin it on somebody else.

01:00:57.740 --> 01:00:58.620
Thought of that, too.

01:00:59.040 --> 01:00:59.700
That isn't all.

01:01:00.670 --> 01:01:02.450
Even if we weren't happy, Helen was my wife.

01:01:04.080 --> 01:01:05.920
The man who killed her isn't going to get away with it.

01:01:07.170 --> 01:01:07.990
He just thinks he is.

01:01:08.800 --> 01:01:10.060
You're talking about Eddie Harwood?

01:01:11.680 --> 01:01:12.760
I didn't mention any names.

01:01:13.410 --> 01:01:14.310
Who else could it be?

01:01:19.200 --> 01:01:20.040
I wouldn't know, would you?

01:01:21.740 --> 01:01:23.160
Seems you know more about it than I do.

01:01:24.960 --> 01:01:25.360
Do I?

01:01:26.900 --> 01:01:29.480
Things like picking me out of the air at a hotel desk.

01:01:31.370 --> 01:01:34.560
You get around, don't you? And your timing's good.

01:01:34.740 --> 01:01:40.320
It was good last night when you picked me up in the rain, was it?

01:01:43.170 --> 01:01:50.360
No, I don't even know your name.

01:01:52.790 --> 01:01:54.170
Johnny, you'll have to trust me.

01:01:54.930 --> 01:01:56.370
I have something to settle, too.

01:01:57.240 --> 01:01:58.460
You'll have to trust me a lot.

01:01:58.930 --> 01:01:59.210
Why?

01:02:00.480 --> 01:02:01.700
I haven't got time to play games.

01:02:03.830 --> 01:02:07.100
Suppose you keep your secrets and I'll keep mine, huh?

01:02:08.630 --> 01:02:14.240
Okay, Johnny, if that's the way you feel about it, coming.

01:02:24.230 --> 01:02:25.990
Turn it down, I tell you!

01:02:26.940 --> 01:02:27.960
Calm down, can't you?

01:02:28.390 --> 01:02:29.370
Other people have to live.

01:02:31.850 --> 01:02:33.550
This headache I got don't calm down.

01:02:35.310 --> 01:02:36.610
Why don't Johnny call up or something?

01:02:37.220 --> 01:02:38.200
Maybe he forgot the number.

01:02:38.820 --> 01:02:39.880
Maybe he doesn't want to take the chance.

01:02:40.000 --> 01:02:41.080
Maybe he's not even in L.A.

01:02:41.260 --> 01:02:42.100
That's three maybes.

01:02:42.220 --> 01:02:43.140
You're not stuck, are you?

01:02:46.080 --> 01:02:49.440
Hey, uh, I used to think of Johnny on the Dodge like a cheap criminal.

01:02:50.430 --> 01:02:52.330
You ought to go straight to Hendrickson and tell him his story.

01:02:53.030 --> 01:02:53.370
Sure.

01:02:54.180 --> 01:02:55.120
Tell it to the cops.

01:02:55.990 --> 01:02:57.190
Maybe you like cops.

01:02:57.940 --> 01:02:58.760
Well, I don't.

01:02:59.490 --> 01:02:59.970
I hate...

01:03:00.700 --> 01:03:03.640
And you better hope you never tell it to the cops either.

01:03:06.400 --> 01:03:07.220
What you need's a drink.

01:03:13.130 --> 01:03:13.750
Let me see.

01:03:14.090 --> 01:03:16.190
I seem to have misplaced your name for the moment.

01:03:16.460 --> 01:03:17.360
Where were you keeping it?

01:03:18.200 --> 01:03:20.060
But you're a friend of John Morrison's, aren't you?

01:03:21.090 --> 01:03:21.890
Never heard of him.

01:03:26.240 --> 01:03:26.660
Come on in.

01:03:33.740 --> 01:03:34.120
Who are you?

01:03:35.470 --> 01:03:36.870
I work over at the Cavendish Court.

01:03:37.390 --> 01:03:38.090
Newell's the name.

01:03:38.250 --> 01:03:39.450
They call me Dad.

01:03:39.900 --> 01:03:40.620
You work at what?

01:03:41.330 --> 01:03:41.570
Well...

01:03:41.570 --> 01:03:42.670
You're the house peeper, ain't you?

01:03:43.630 --> 01:03:44.830
Yeah, some folks call me that.

01:03:46.470 --> 01:03:49.110
I don't suppose you gentlemen know where Mr. Morrison is, do you?

01:03:49.420 --> 01:03:50.560
Would we be likely to tell you?

01:03:52.390 --> 01:03:53.400
No, I suppose not.

01:03:55.000 --> 01:03:57.980
Would information about his movements be worth anything to you?

01:03:58.610 --> 01:03:59.910
Depends on what the information is.

01:04:01.120 --> 01:04:04.210
Well, information ain't always so easy to get.

01:04:04.430 --> 01:04:05.830
Quit stalling. Where did you see Johnny?

01:04:06.790 --> 01:04:08.450
Instead, I did see him, so far.

01:04:08.610 --> 01:04:11.750
This guy's looking for a piece of change.

01:04:11.930 --> 01:04:12.840
Did you just think of that?

01:04:13.510 --> 01:04:16.150
Well, as a matter of fact, it was a long walk over here.

01:04:16.810 --> 01:04:18.870
Why don't you call a couple of those cops you're so fond of?

01:04:18.950 --> 01:04:20.010
He's been cheating on their terms.

01:04:20.110 --> 01:04:22.390
Oh, now, wait a minute, gentlemen. You got me all wrong.

01:04:22.570 --> 01:04:23.290
Would that be possible?

01:04:23.800 --> 01:04:26.880
I happen to be going by Mr. Harwood's hotel this evening.

01:04:26.900 --> 01:04:28.060
Oh, you put the bite on Harwood, too.

01:04:28.140 --> 01:04:29.000
I resent that.

01:04:30.090 --> 01:04:32.290
I saw Morrison go into the hotel and cross over the desk.

01:04:32.510 --> 01:04:32.830
Then what?

01:04:33.360 --> 01:04:34.820
I didn't have time to wait for any more.

01:04:35.240 --> 01:04:36.540
He was standing at the desk when I left.

01:04:36.700 --> 01:04:37.320
I had to get to work.

01:04:37.480 --> 01:04:39.180
The guy really likes his work.

01:04:39.530 --> 01:04:39.930
And how?

01:04:40.840 --> 01:04:41.700
Where does Harwood live?

01:04:42.490 --> 01:04:43.690
Granada Towers in Wilshire.

01:04:43.850 --> 01:04:45.070
You know everything, don't you?

01:04:45.810 --> 01:04:46.910
Oh, I get around.

01:04:47.840 --> 01:04:48.780
Is that all you've got to tell us?

01:04:49.880 --> 01:04:50.720
So far it is.

01:04:58.700 --> 01:04:59.020
Thanks.

01:05:01.080 --> 01:05:07.620
Nights, Mr. Harwood usually goes to his club, the Blue Dahlia, if that's of any interest to you.

01:05:16.100 --> 01:05:17.260
Haven't I seen you before?

01:05:19.100 --> 01:05:19.620
Before what?

01:05:20.460 --> 01:05:22.040
Seen it to me last night in the rain.

01:05:23.640 --> 01:05:25.920
Oh, of course, I could be mistaken.

01:05:27.560 --> 01:05:27.880
Good night.

01:05:34.890 --> 01:05:37.590
Mr. Harwood, please. Mrs. Harwood calling.

01:05:41.040 --> 01:05:41.280
Eddie?

01:05:42.590 --> 01:05:46.260
Yes, it's me. I've changed my mind about something.

01:05:47.130 --> 01:05:48.130
Do you want to take me out tonight?

01:06:01.240 --> 01:06:02.000
Find what you wanted.

01:06:07.510 --> 01:06:08.630
You look good in a uniform.

01:06:10.260 --> 01:06:11.000
Nice kid, too.

01:06:11.300 --> 01:06:11.560
Yours?

01:06:17.700 --> 01:06:19.000
Why didn't you tell me you was hot?

01:06:19.350 --> 01:06:20.910
I've taken care of lots of hot boys.

01:06:21.970 --> 01:06:23.370
All it takes is a little of that.

01:06:23.570 --> 01:06:27.310
What makes you think I'm hot?

01:06:28.710 --> 01:06:29.970
You ain't talking to one of them ch-

01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:43.980
heist guys like them mugs that brought you here i've been in this business a long time jimmy moore

01:06:43.980 --> 01:06:52.040
huh seems like i read somewhere it could have been in the paper about a guy named johnny morrison

01:06:53.250 --> 01:06:55.870
cops wanted to talk to on account his wife got broke

01:07:00.000 --> 01:07:03.700
Suit yourself.

01:07:08.730 --> 01:07:10.710
Maybe I better keep this while you think things out.

01:08:19.840 --> 01:08:29.820
who's he put him on you leo and a joint over in santa monica a guy come in there tonight

01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:37.370
registered as jimmy moore get the initials jm he's a navy flyer that mean anything to you

01:08:37.370 --> 01:08:52.020
is he there now moved out on you you don't seem to have much to sell do you corelli i'll take care

01:08:52.020 --> 01:08:59.970
of you so long corelli there's certainly a

01:09:00.030 --> 01:09:01.070
Hard man to catch up with.

01:09:01.530 --> 01:09:01.850
Am I?

01:09:03.890 --> 01:09:04.990
Nice to know you, Mr. Boer.

01:09:06.020 --> 01:09:07.020
That is your name, isn't it?

01:09:08.450 --> 01:09:09.750
You know my name and why I'm here.

01:09:10.900 --> 01:09:12.560
I don't, but you can tell me while I finish dressing.

01:09:14.680 --> 01:09:16.560
If I were in your shoes, I'd be 500 miles away.

01:09:17.480 --> 01:09:18.940
Half the cops in L.A. are looking for you.

01:09:19.810 --> 01:09:20.370
Only half.

01:09:22.890 --> 01:09:25.170
All I have to do is pick up the telephone, you go out of here in handcuffs.

01:09:26.610 --> 01:09:27.030
Why don't you?

01:09:29.340 --> 01:09:29.980
Don't happen to be that kind.

01:09:30.000 --> 01:09:34.020
What kind of a rat? What kind of a rat are you?

01:09:36.480 --> 01:09:37.780
I'm not a police informer, anyway.

01:09:42.790 --> 01:09:46.500
Neither am I, so far.

01:09:47.510 --> 01:09:53.140
Whatever that means. You treat yourself a pretty tough boy, don't you?

01:09:54.980 --> 01:09:56.660
Tough enough to find out who killed my wife.

01:09:57.920 --> 01:09:59.600
Everybody seems to think you killed her.

01:10:01.660 --> 01:10:06.040
Not quite everybody. I think you killed her.

01:10:08.680 --> 01:10:09.480
Don't be a dope.

01:10:10.500 --> 01:10:12.140
Just because I took Helen out a couple of times

01:10:12.140 --> 01:10:14.280
and you put on that injured husband, I...

01:10:15.490 --> 01:10:16.590
What's a dope in your book?

01:10:19.600 --> 01:10:21.360
A guy without sense enough to get out while he can

01:10:21.360 --> 01:10:24.640
and hole up in some quiet place where people don't know you.

01:10:33.420 --> 01:10:34.380
Nobody knows me here.

01:10:34.600 --> 01:10:35.460
They soon will.

01:10:36.930 --> 01:10:37.890
Easy for you to call.

01:10:40.300 --> 01:10:41.740
Me, I'd have to call long distance.

01:10:42.380 --> 01:10:43.360
I still don't get it.

01:10:44.130 --> 01:10:44.350
No.

01:10:46.620 --> 01:10:48.080
How long has it been since you were in New Jersey?

01:10:52.810 --> 01:10:53.450
I don't get that either.

01:10:59.040 --> 01:10:59.920
Just why New Jersey?

01:11:00.000 --> 01:11:07.450
Are you going to answer the door or let them break it down?

01:11:19.150 --> 01:11:19.590
Get you a drink?

01:11:20.690 --> 01:11:22.150
Not now, thanks. I'll wait.

01:11:22.450 --> 01:11:23.010
I'll just be a minute.

01:11:26.890 --> 01:11:27.770
Made you change your mind.

01:11:29.230 --> 01:11:29.890
Still have trouble.

01:11:30.000 --> 01:11:43.980
with your bow tie. Oh, I'm sorry. This is Mr. Moore. Mr. Moore, my wife. How do you do, Mr. Moore?

01:11:45.260 --> 01:11:59.700
I'll get my coat. Fix yourself a drink. Well, why don't you say it? I might just as well have told you.

01:12:00.220 --> 01:12:01.920
He would have read it in the papers tomorrow anyway.

01:12:07.750 --> 01:12:09.410
Didn't save myself much, did I?

01:12:09.550 --> 01:12:18.100
You don't owe me an explanation.

01:12:19.180 --> 01:12:20.360
I didn't want it this way.

01:12:21.600 --> 01:12:22.640
I'll bet you didn't.

01:12:25.650 --> 01:12:27.670
Johnny, don't you realize you're in danger here?

01:12:28.760 --> 01:12:29.860
That isn't what worries me.

01:12:31.630 --> 01:12:36.420
I came here to do something, but you fixed that, too.

01:12:39.730 --> 01:12:40.030
Johnny!

01:12:41.980 --> 01:12:42.860
So long, baby.

01:12:50.700 --> 01:12:51.740
George, will you hurry up?

01:12:51.820 --> 01:12:53.660
You boys going somewhere?

01:12:54.810 --> 01:12:56.630
For crying out loud, come in here.

01:12:56.750 --> 01:12:57.270
Hey, George!

01:12:58.260 --> 01:12:58.620
Johnny!

01:12:59.570 --> 01:12:59.890
See you.

01:13:00.600 --> 01:13:03.460
What a heard you turned out to be. Where you been keepin' yourselves?

01:13:03.680 --> 01:13:06.300
Well, I tried to call you, but some strange voice answered the phone.

01:13:06.400 --> 01:13:08.700
That was the cops. They took us down for questioning. Are you all right?

01:13:09.330 --> 01:13:12.200
Depends on what you mean by all right. Here you got a drink.

01:13:12.430 --> 01:13:14.210
You bet. You want it in a glass or a funnel?

01:13:14.750 --> 01:13:15.190
As usual.

01:13:15.410 --> 01:13:17.520
Bourbon straight with a bourbon chaser. Come on.

01:13:23.820 --> 01:13:28.340
Me? You guys did all right for yourself.

01:13:28.630 --> 01:13:29.610
Hey, I'll pour that into you.

01:13:37.580 --> 01:13:39.280
What are you going to do, Johnny? Any ideas?

01:13:39.960 --> 01:13:42.480
It's pretty obvious. Much choice.

01:13:42.680 --> 01:13:44.200
You're not going to give yourself up to the cops.

01:13:45.520 --> 01:13:45.880
Why not?

01:13:46.260 --> 01:13:48.670
Johnny's right. The longer he hides out, the tougher it'll be.

01:13:48.730 --> 01:13:49.670
And he can't hide out forever.

01:13:49.970 --> 01:13:51.570
No, not if somebody rats on him, he can't.

01:13:52.110 --> 01:13:53.090
Meaning me, I suppose.

01:13:53.840 --> 01:13:55.360
Johnny, did that housekeeper see you downstairs?

01:13:57.140 --> 01:13:57.460
Housekeeper?

01:13:58.060 --> 01:13:59.160
The one at the Cavendish court.

01:13:59.340 --> 01:13:59.980
He was here just a...

01:14:00.440 --> 01:14:01.940
He saw you go into Harwood's hotel.

01:14:03.730 --> 01:14:04.810
I wonder what he was doing there.

01:14:05.300 --> 01:14:06.360
Maybe there was a buck in it.

01:14:12.280 --> 01:14:14.560
George, what do you think my chances are if I give myself up?

01:14:15.750 --> 01:14:17.610
With a record like yours and after what happened,

01:14:17.810 --> 01:14:19.390
no jury in the world would convict you.

01:14:19.730 --> 01:14:21.010
We're not gonna take that chance, Johnny.

01:14:21.170 --> 01:14:22.210
You and me are gonna scram out of here.

01:14:22.290 --> 01:14:23.610
The cops won't be looking for two guys.

01:14:26.370 --> 01:14:29.980
Wait a minute. You boys think I can...

01:14:30.000 --> 01:14:34.420
Well, it doesn't make any difference what we think.

01:14:35.480 --> 01:14:35.800
Legally...

01:14:35.800 --> 01:14:39.900
Legally? You can skip the rest of it.

01:14:42.220 --> 01:14:42.660
Don't be a fool.

01:14:42.660 --> 01:14:43.520
Come on, you're out of the way.

01:14:43.700 --> 01:14:45.480
Wait a minute, Johnny, it don't matter to me what you've done.

01:14:55.330 --> 01:14:56.130
Johnny, wait a minute!

01:15:05.370 --> 01:15:06.670
Well, I hope you're satisfied.

01:15:10.070 --> 01:15:18.110
Morrison, expecting this, haven't you, Mr. Morrison?

01:15:19.550 --> 01:15:20.970
How much dough did you give that house paper?

01:15:21.510 --> 01:15:21.810
What?

01:15:22.320 --> 01:15:24.580
All you bought yourself was a pinch. Take a look. They got him.

01:15:30.920 --> 01:15:44.470
Hey, this isn't the way to headquarters.

01:15:44.750 --> 01:15:52.730
Let me see that badge again.

01:16:01.950 --> 01:16:02.910
This is a courtesy badge.

01:16:04.380 --> 01:16:05.520
You got courtesy, didn't you?

01:16:23.660 --> 01:16:24.380
Can you handle them alone?

01:16:24.940 --> 01:16:25.180
Yeah.

01:16:41.200 --> 01:16:42.140
I didn't hit him too hard.

01:16:42.600 --> 01:16:43.420
We might need him for bait.

01:16:57.680 --> 01:16:58.040
Hold it.

01:16:59.580 --> 01:16:59.980
Give it to him.

01:17:03.900 --> 01:17:04.780
Nice guy, huh?

01:17:26.820 --> 01:17:28.670
It's easy to...

01:17:35.350 --> 01:17:39.220
Mr. Howard, there are two men asking to see you.

01:17:39.850 --> 01:17:40.690
Any idea what they want?

01:17:41.150 --> 01:17:42.230
I'm sorry they wouldn't tell me.

01:17:44.540 --> 01:17:45.380
Suppose they'll tell me?

01:17:48.710 --> 01:17:51.190
These nightclub monkeys do all right for themselves, don't they, George?

01:17:51.350 --> 01:17:52.350
Looks like there's a living in it.

01:17:54.420 --> 01:17:55.140
You wish to see me?

01:17:55.640 --> 01:17:57.180
We're friends of Johnny Morrison's.

01:17:58.460 --> 01:17:58.600
Well?

01:17:59.680 --> 01:17:59.980
You've heard...

01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:00.700
You've heard of them, haven't you?

01:18:02.400 --> 01:18:03.200
Come to my office.

01:18:10.520 --> 01:18:11.140
Have a seat.

01:18:12.240 --> 01:18:12.840
Stand up.

01:18:14.880 --> 01:18:18.010
What's on your mind?

01:18:18.710 --> 01:18:21.570
About half an hour ago, Johnny was picked up outside our apartment...

01:18:21.570 --> 01:18:22.990
...by a couple of plainclothes men.

01:18:23.980 --> 01:18:25.420
That's the best thing that could have happened to him, isn't it?

01:18:25.560 --> 01:18:27.100
That's what we thought, half an hour ago.

01:18:27.430 --> 01:18:29.770
Only they didn't happen to be plainclothes men. We checked it.

01:18:30.030 --> 01:18:36.830
quarters. And are you surprised? Maybe you ought to tell me what you're talking about. This is a guy

01:18:36.830 --> 01:18:41.600
you really got to draw a picture for, George. Now take it easy. Take it easy. That's all you

01:18:41.600 --> 01:18:48.460
do. Take it easy. What does it get you? What did it get Johnny? Maybe you can

01:18:48.460 --> 01:18:57.760
answer that funny face. Before you answer that, get this through your head. If anything

01:18:57.760 --> 01:18:59.980
happens to Johnny, you're looking at a couple of guys who'll...

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:02.020
We'll spend a lot of time taking care of whoever did it.

01:19:04.320 --> 01:19:05.560
I'll remember that if it seems important.

01:19:05.760 --> 01:19:06.760
We'll take care of that too.

01:19:08.540 --> 01:19:11.160
Hello, Captain Hendrickson, put him on.

01:19:11.340 --> 01:19:12.900
These guys are full of nifties, George.

01:19:14.730 --> 01:19:17.300
Yeah, just a minute.

01:19:21.540 --> 01:19:21.880
Yes, Captain.

01:19:30.700 --> 01:19:36.070
I'll be right down, Captain. I'm leaving now, okay?

01:19:37.500 --> 01:19:38.480
Well, wait till you get back.

01:19:39.740 --> 01:19:40.420
Make yourselves at home.

01:19:44.420 --> 01:19:45.520
Yeah, that's really something, ain't it?

01:19:45.980 --> 01:19:46.680
You think you busted it?

01:19:46.930 --> 01:19:48.830
I could be. The table did plenty hard enough.

01:19:50.000 --> 01:19:50.920
Yeah, he put it in here.

01:19:52.100 --> 01:19:53.500
Put some salt in it. It might help.

01:19:58.060 --> 01:19:58.940
That's real good.

01:20:02.520 --> 01:20:03.720
at a time of just in case.

01:20:48.330 --> 01:20:56.810
How much dough was in the billfold?

01:20:57.420 --> 01:20:58.220
What billfold?

01:20:58.600 --> 01:20:59.600
Pretty good fountain pen, too.

01:21:00.090 --> 01:21:01.800
Huh? What else did you get?

01:21:03.270 --> 01:21:05.230
Nothing. Come on, hand it over.

01:21:08.480 --> 01:21:08.780
Okay.

01:21:25.810 --> 01:21:27.390
Fixing this business the same as any other.

01:21:39.660 --> 01:21:41.520
Excuse me, I thought my husband was in here.

01:21:42.050 --> 01:21:43.140
Hmm, give a look.

01:21:43.870 --> 01:21:44.450
Horwood's babe.

01:21:45.150 --> 01:21:46.530
I bet she caused plenty, huh, George?

01:21:46.790 --> 01:21:49.130
How much would it cost to get you to button your lip just once?

01:21:50.020 --> 01:21:52.210
I'm sorry, Mr. Horwood went out.

01:21:57.650 --> 01:21:58.950
You're George and Buzz, aren't you?

01:21:59.660 --> 01:21:59.900
Female.

01:22:00.980 --> 01:22:02.280
Johnny told me about you.

01:22:02.760 --> 01:22:03.860
Why would he tell you anything?

01:22:04.950 --> 01:22:06.730
It just so happens I'm a friend of his, too.

01:22:07.200 --> 01:22:08.820
Since when? We only hit town yesterday.

01:22:09.930 --> 01:22:12.330
How long does it take to become a friend of Johnny Morrison's?

01:22:15.050 --> 01:22:18.410
Oh, excuse me, Captain Hendrickson's on the phone asking for Mr. Harwood.

01:22:18.980 --> 01:22:19.640
What shall I tell him?

01:22:19.800 --> 01:22:22.800
Tell him to go soak his head. Get out of here and close that door!

01:22:23.400 --> 01:22:25.280
I gotta listen any more of that monkey musical!

01:22:25.580 --> 01:22:29.670
Mr. Harwood's on his way to the captain's office.

01:22:30.440 --> 01:22:31.380
Just tell him he's left.

01:22:32.130 --> 01:22:32.550
Yes, ma'am.

01:22:37.560 --> 01:22:40.150
It's a shell fragment right above the air.

01:22:40.720 --> 01:22:42.860
They're playing over and over and over again.

01:22:43.920 --> 01:22:48.440
Like it was the only record they had in one of those ritzy bungalows.

01:22:49.600 --> 01:22:51.480
Buzz, what are you talking about?

01:22:55.120 --> 01:22:55.440
I don't know.

01:23:04.730 --> 01:23:05.650
What are you doing that for?

01:23:07.250 --> 01:23:07.530
What?

01:23:08.430 --> 01:23:09.450
Picking at that flower.

01:23:10.830 --> 01:23:11.450
I don't like it.

01:23:18.420 --> 01:23:19.100
Say, that's funny.

01:23:19.320 --> 01:23:24.690
That's the same monkey music they kept playing in the apartment next door.

01:23:26.560 --> 01:23:28.780
All day long, beating in my head.

01:23:32.140 --> 01:23:33.480
You gotta pull yourself together, fella.

01:23:36.630 --> 01:23:39.190
It wasn't next door either. It was someplace else.

01:23:43.100 --> 01:23:45.080
The music was right in the same room with us.

01:23:46.900 --> 01:23:51.880
She kept picking at that flower, just like you were doing.

01:23:53.920 --> 01:23:57.710
Only she wouldn't stop. She kept right on doing it.

01:26:01.310 --> 01:26:02.530
Hello, this is Mr. Hallward. Is Paul there?

01:26:04.640 --> 01:26:08.010
What? Give me that again. Slow.

01:26:12.140 --> 01:26:13.390
Okay. Tell him to relax.

01:26:15.190 --> 01:26:15.710
I'll be right back.

01:26:15.790 --> 01:26:18.540
Still playing the hot shot, huh?

01:26:18.620 --> 01:26:21.970
Looks disappointed.

01:26:22.270 --> 01:26:25.570
The boys did their best, Mr. Bauer.

01:26:31.596 --> 01:26:33.596
Mind telling me how you found out?

01:26:33.708 --> 01:26:35.708
Recognize that photograph on the floor?

01:26:36.300 --> 01:26:37.500
Read what's on the back of it.

01:26:42.828 --> 01:26:43.828
That would be a hell-in.

01:26:45.324 --> 01:26:47.104
She wasn't the girl to throw away this kind of information.

01:26:48.108 --> 01:26:49.948
Why didn't you make sure of that before you killed her?

01:26:50.604 --> 01:26:51.524
In a hotel bungalow?

01:26:52.620 --> 01:26:53.400
With a 45.

01:26:55.820 --> 01:26:57.200
I could have arranged things better than that.

01:26:57.804 --> 01:26:58.784
Like you arrange this?

01:27:02.332 --> 01:27:03.932
This could have stood a little more polished, too.

01:27:05.724 --> 01:27:06.284
Just a cigarette.

01:27:14.780 --> 01:27:15.440
Maybe you're right at that.

01:27:18.780 --> 01:27:20.020
Not much of a hot shot after all.

01:27:24.924 --> 01:27:26.404
Such a nice, clean start I had.

01:27:26.460 --> 01:27:28.460
so

01:27:30.860 --> 01:27:33.880
Helping another wild kid shoot a bank messenger back in Per Se.

01:27:35.340 --> 01:27:36.100
And for free.

01:27:36.908 --> 01:27:37.908
Didn't have a dime on him.

01:27:39.532 --> 01:27:42.532
And I spent the next 15 years trying to kid myself it never happened.

01:27:45.484 --> 01:27:46.644
It gets on a wall plat.

01:27:47.052 --> 01:27:47.632
Nightclub.

01:27:49.260 --> 01:27:50.300
I even marry a girl.

01:27:53.580 --> 01:27:55.540
Girl oughtn't have given me the time of the day.

01:28:00.000 --> 01:28:01.000
That's how I end up.

01:28:05.116 --> 01:28:08.116
What makes it even worse is the cops aren't interested in either of us anymore.

01:28:09.276 --> 01:28:10.316
They've already got that killer.

01:28:13.148 --> 01:28:13.448
Man.

01:28:14.364 --> 01:28:16.144
caught up with him at the Blue Dahlia a little while ago.

01:28:17.564 --> 01:28:18.324
One of your buddies.

01:28:19.324 --> 01:28:20.064
He just confessed.

01:28:25.852 --> 01:28:26.852
What are you trying to give me?

01:28:28.348 --> 01:28:28.808
There's the phone.

01:29:00.090 --> 01:29:05.590
No, okay, so she did give me a little dough once in a while to keep my mouth shut.

01:29:05.710 --> 01:29:06.790
What's so wrong with that?

01:29:06.980 --> 01:29:08.040
That's the last I got.

01:29:08.830 --> 01:29:09.550
Newell, come here.

01:29:15.000 --> 01:29:18.100
Are you positive this is the man you saw go into the bungalow with Mrs. Morrison?

01:29:18.420 --> 01:29:20.820
I already told you I did, didn't I? Ain't that enough?

01:29:21.540 --> 01:29:23.240
It's our business to know what's enough.

01:29:23.640 --> 01:29:27.290
Take it easy. Now let's get back to the shot you heard...

01:29:27.290 --> 01:29:29.450
...seeing you finally made your mind up to tell us about it.

01:29:30.000 --> 01:29:32.820
Wait a minute, Captain Hendrickson. I ain't trying to hold anything back.

01:29:33.260 --> 01:29:34.480
It might have been backfire.

01:29:34.924 --> 01:29:36.324
It ain't always so easy to tell.

01:29:36.684 --> 01:29:37.484
What time was it?

01:29:38.540 --> 01:29:40.720
Here's, I can figure, about ten minutes to eight.

01:29:41.484 --> 01:29:43.164
And what time did you say this man got home?

01:29:43.468 --> 01:29:44.088
I didn't say.

01:29:44.588 --> 01:29:45.748
I didn't even say he went out.

01:29:46.156 --> 01:29:48.496
Quit trying to cover up for me, George. Give them what they want.

01:29:48.636 --> 01:29:50.796
What for? To back up the evidence of a cheap blackmailer?

01:29:51.404 --> 01:29:52.204
Hey, just a minute.

01:29:52.204 --> 01:29:52.704
Shut up!

01:29:53.068 --> 01:29:53.788
And sit down.

01:29:55.244 --> 01:29:55.884
Over there.

01:30:01.756 --> 01:30:02.336
Come on, son.

01:30:03.292 --> 01:30:06.172
You just about told us you killed her. Why not give us the rest of it?

01:30:06.460 --> 01:30:09.300
Why do you have to keep pounding at him? What more do you want him to say?

01:30:10.108 --> 01:30:12.308
It's got to make sense to us, too, Mrs. Harwood.

01:30:14.908 --> 01:30:16.268
You didn't go there to kill her.

01:30:16.764 --> 01:30:18.244
You'd never even seen her before.

01:30:20.028 --> 01:30:21.668
What did she do that got you going?

01:30:23.356 --> 01:30:24.136
things she said.

01:30:25.788 --> 01:30:26.448
what she was.

01:30:28.668 --> 01:30:29.588
What she did to Johnny.

01:30:31.280 --> 01:30:35.350
She didn't even care. All she did was pick at that flower.

01:30:35.570 --> 01:30:40.250
And the gun lying right there in the chair, asking you to use it.

01:30:40.350 --> 01:30:43.490
My head hurts. I don't remember so good.

01:30:43.750 --> 01:30:44.960
Sure you're in pain.

01:30:46.530 --> 01:30:59.960
Johnny's wife we're talking about. You remember Johnny's wife all right. Johnny. Johnny. George. George, where's Johnny? Why ain't Johnny here? He'd know I wouldn't.

01:31:00.000 --> 01:31:03.780
mean to do a thing like that? No, why wouldn't you? All you had to do was grab hold of the gun,

01:31:03.840 --> 01:31:07.020
jab it against her heart, and squeeze the trigger. That's the way it was, wasn't it?

01:31:08.080 --> 01:31:11.920
Don't give out! Don't try to dummy up on us. That's the way it was, wasn't it?

01:31:12.690 --> 01:31:14.560
Sounds like you said it all. Johnny!

01:31:16.560 --> 01:31:19.650
Hello, Mr. Morrison. About time we got together.

01:31:26.200 --> 01:31:29.030
Nobody's gonna get hurt with this except maybe me. Buzz.

01:31:34.988 --> 01:31:35.888
Okay, Buzz, light it.

01:31:38.188 --> 01:31:38.988
Johnny, you're crazy.

01:31:39.820 --> 01:31:41.100
Let him alone, give him back that gun.

01:31:41.280 --> 01:31:42.080
He can't do it anymore.

01:31:42.444 --> 01:31:43.544
He can deal with his eyes shut.

01:31:44.300 --> 01:31:44.940
On your feet, Buzz.

01:31:47.436 --> 01:31:48.436
Only a fear I said.

01:31:51.788 --> 01:31:52.688
Now give him back that gun.

01:32:00.160 --> 01:32:01.420
All right, fella, light it up.

01:32:08.420 --> 01:32:21.640
Okay, Skipper. I did it. I did it, didn't I, Johnny?

01:32:22.200 --> 01:32:22.840
Sure you did.

01:32:24.150 --> 01:32:27.020
Chadwick against the heart, huh? Still buying that?

01:32:27.930 --> 01:32:29.840
I have to. That's how she was killed.

01:32:30.830 --> 01:32:31.670
What says he killed her?

01:32:32.660 --> 01:32:33.600
It was his own idea.

01:32:35.450 --> 01:32:36.290
Who sold him the idea?

01:32:36.800 --> 01:32:37.200
I did.

01:32:39.220 --> 01:32:40.140
Would be me, wouldn't it?

01:32:41.900 --> 01:32:42.860
Would you mind telling me how?

01:32:47.950 --> 01:32:50.830
He got terribly upset when I began to pull the petals from this flower.

01:32:53.350 --> 01:32:54.710
This is beginning to make sense.

01:32:56.200 --> 01:32:57.560
He must have seen Helen do that, too.

01:32:59.300 --> 01:32:59.920
It was my gun.

01:33:00.000 --> 01:33:02.650
Helen and I were calling.

01:33:04.500 --> 01:33:04.960
We were loud.

01:33:07.990 --> 01:33:08.510
You knew that.

01:33:08.610 --> 01:33:09.070
You heard us.

01:33:10.600 --> 01:33:12.300
Why didn't you tell them about coming through that door?

01:33:13.100 --> 01:33:13.780
Sure I did.

01:33:14.430 --> 01:33:15.930
I kind of had to, didn't I, Mr. Morrison?

01:33:18.840 --> 01:33:20.660
Well, you got a fall guy standing right in front of you.

01:33:20.920 --> 01:33:21.600
What more do you want?

01:33:22.350 --> 01:33:25.170
I just happened to be dumb enough to want to get the right fall guy.

01:33:25.690 --> 01:33:28.030
When your wife was killed, you were 50 miles north of here.

01:33:28.420 --> 01:33:29.280
Let's you out, doesn't it?

01:33:30.280 --> 01:33:34.180
That's Mrs. Harwood out, too. Makes things a little tough for us, doesn't it?

01:33:35.070 --> 01:33:38.610
Yeah, you're right out on the limb. It's all you've got left, just to pick on him.

01:33:39.240 --> 01:33:40.940
We've still got Harwood, if we can find him.

01:33:41.280 --> 01:33:42.220
Well, you can count Harwood out.

01:33:42.450 --> 01:33:43.070
That's interesting.

01:33:43.800 --> 01:33:45.980
And if you know where Leo's ranch is, maybe you'd better go take a look.

01:33:46.380 --> 01:33:49.730
Think you can arrange that? Any further details?

01:33:50.490 --> 01:33:52.110
Now, look, Captain, I'm not trying to run your business.

01:33:52.350 --> 01:33:53.910
You're doing fine. I'm not proud.

01:33:54.090 --> 01:33:57.610
You were swelling there a minute ago, Buzz.

01:33:58.490 --> 01:33:59.980
Ha! Still got their old...

01:34:01.180 --> 01:34:02.620
Sure you have, but you gotta have a lot more.

01:34:03.460 --> 01:34:04.400
Come on, tell me the part that counts.

01:34:05.700 --> 01:34:05.980
Counts?

01:34:07.960 --> 01:34:08.940
Yeah, come on, come on.

01:34:09.930 --> 01:34:11.390
That's what they keep saying.

01:34:12.380 --> 01:34:14.620
I hit that match just like I used to, didn't I, Johnny?

01:34:15.240 --> 01:34:16.920
He can't remember, Johnny. He just doesn't know.

01:34:17.830 --> 01:34:21.010
Well, what's the matter with me, Johnny?

01:34:21.250 --> 01:34:23.070
There's nothing wrong with you, Buzz. You just gotta think.

01:34:23.210 --> 01:34:24.130
You gotta remember, that's all.

01:34:24.810 --> 01:34:27.390
All right, now, for me, for me, what happened in the bungalow?

01:34:28.790 --> 01:34:29.070
Come on.

01:34:30.060 --> 01:34:30.440
That's right.

01:34:30.720 --> 01:34:31.760
Yeah, there was a bungalow, Johnny.

01:34:32.640 --> 01:34:38.520
Yeah, and she kept picking at that flower, Johnny,

01:34:38.700 --> 01:34:41.050
just like that one over there.

01:34:41.540 --> 01:34:41.740
Yeah.

01:34:43.300 --> 01:34:45.860
And I was raining, and I...

01:34:46.550 --> 01:34:47.790
Come on, what happened, Buzz? Come on.

01:34:48.700 --> 01:34:51.660
My head music was beating, Johnny.

01:34:51.940 --> 01:34:55.100
Beating, beating, beating, beating, beating, beating.

01:34:55.730 --> 01:34:56.210
Music in my...

01:34:57.130 --> 01:34:59.130
Johnny, you don't think I did it, do you, Johnny?

01:34:59.660 --> 01:34:59.980
Is it right?

01:35:00.000 --> 01:35:00.340
What do you hear?

01:35:01.180 --> 01:35:02.640
Just the speaker from the dance floor.

01:35:03.080 --> 01:35:03.600
Turn it on.

01:35:05.060 --> 01:35:24.730
She did buy me a drink.

01:35:25.790 --> 01:35:26.470
What's wrong with that?

01:35:27.760 --> 01:35:29.980
I didn't even know who she was until she started talking about...

01:35:30.000 --> 01:35:33.590
Johnny, will you cut that music out?

01:35:33.690 --> 01:35:34.750
Go on with the rest of it, Buzz.

01:35:35.180 --> 01:35:36.000
Why did you kill her?

01:35:38.380 --> 01:35:39.380
Who says I killed her?

01:35:40.700 --> 01:35:42.020
You can't hand me that stuff.

01:35:42.700 --> 01:35:43.420
Not even you.

01:35:44.200 --> 01:35:45.800
I wouldn't dirty my hands on her.

01:35:53.730 --> 01:35:54.670
I didn't mean that, Johnny.

01:35:56.270 --> 01:35:57.470
I just had to get out of there.

01:35:58.830 --> 01:35:59.630
I couldn't take it anymore.

01:36:01.370 --> 01:36:09.490
she called me back but i just kept right on going i don't know where i guess i must have

01:36:09.490 --> 01:36:14.640
gone home that's where i went wasn't it george he was wet enough to have walked all the way and he

01:36:14.640 --> 01:36:19.480
got home just three minutes past eight are you satisfied you could have told us that a long time

01:36:19.480 --> 01:36:24.070
ago i guess you know why i didn't i wasn't sure enough when that shot was fired are you sure now

01:36:24.070 --> 01:36:29.840
you got a witness haven't you a witness you yourself called a cheap blackmailer now

01:36:30.000 --> 01:36:33.220
Just a minute. I could be called that once too often.

01:36:33.670 --> 01:36:35.250
You be sure to tell us when to duck.

01:36:36.140 --> 01:36:38.120
What makes you so top-heavy all of a sudden?

01:36:38.540 --> 01:36:41.120
For all anybody here knows, you could have killed Mrs. Morrison yourself.

01:36:41.380 --> 01:36:42.720
Except that you fixed the time.

01:36:44.000 --> 01:36:45.820
Well, maybe I kind of made a mistake there.

01:36:46.550 --> 01:36:49.030
Five or ten minutes either way, pretty hard to tell.

01:36:49.850 --> 01:36:52.010
I was kind of busy keeping the rain off my neck.

01:36:53.010 --> 01:36:54.550
I ain't the wristwatch type.

01:36:55.560 --> 01:36:57.980
That umbrella of yours must have got pretty wet last night.

01:36:58.480 --> 01:36:59.400
That's what I bought it for.

01:37:00.120 --> 01:37:03.940
You ought to have left it on the porch instead of letting it drip all over Mrs. Morrison's carpet.

01:37:04.140 --> 01:37:06.280
I did leave it on the porch. That is, I...

01:37:06.280 --> 01:37:10.470
All right. Might as well wrap it up for tonight. We don't seem to be getting anyplace.

01:37:11.320 --> 01:37:14.800
Will won't sign statements from all of you, but tomorrow will be time enough.

01:37:16.430 --> 01:37:18.260
Yeah, I got to get back the job myself.

01:37:20.150 --> 01:37:23.130
Well, good night, all. No hard feelings, I hope.

01:37:24.920 --> 01:37:28.340
Oh, Captain, wish you'd put in a good word for me with the hotel manager.

01:37:28.540 --> 01:37:29.900
He's kind of sore at me.

01:37:31.210 --> 01:37:33.250
Surely not for blackmailing the guests.

01:37:35.160 --> 01:37:35.540
All right.

01:37:37.590 --> 01:37:39.750
You don't really think you're going out that door, do you?

01:37:45.900 --> 01:37:46.420
I'm getting there.

01:37:47.530 --> 01:37:50.170
How much did you up the ante on her when her husband came home?

01:37:51.380 --> 01:37:52.440
What did she threaten to do?

01:37:52.940 --> 01:37:53.680
Get you fired?

01:37:53.880 --> 01:37:56.760
Or was she going to have Harwood's friends give you the treatment?

01:37:58.390 --> 01:37:59.970
Maybe she was going to blow a hole in your...

01:38:00.000 --> 01:38:05.580
herself and she wouldn't know how to handle that kind of a gun all you had to do was grab it out

01:38:05.580 --> 01:38:14.800
of her hand i guess even a very cheap blackmailer could do that cheap huh sure cigar and a drink

01:38:14.800 --> 01:38:20.970
and a couple of dirty bucks that's all it cost to buy me that's what she thought found out a

01:38:20.970 --> 01:38:25.900
little different didn't she maybe i could get tired of being pushed around by cops and hotel

01:38:25.900 --> 01:38:29.920
managers and ritzy dames and bungalows maybe

01:38:30.000 --> 01:38:31.860
I could cost a little something just for once.

01:38:32.720 --> 01:38:46.850
And if I do end up in a slab, boy, am I sunk.

01:38:47.510 --> 01:38:48.950
And that was one of the easy ones.

01:38:49.410 --> 01:38:50.430
Must be getting old.

01:38:50.960 --> 01:38:53.080
Felt kind of sorry for the old gent at that.

01:38:57.940 --> 01:38:58.600
Thanks, Bill.

01:38:58.780 --> 01:38:59.600
You're welcome, Mrs. Howard.

01:39:00.000 --> 01:39:07.900
We seem to be saying goodbye again. Won't be so difficult this time, I guess.

01:39:10.380 --> 01:39:12.800
Last night, when I made myself walk out on you, remember?

01:39:14.270 --> 01:39:16.800
I said every guy had seen you before, somewhere.

01:39:18.210 --> 01:39:18.790
I remember.

01:39:19.800 --> 01:39:21.020
But the trick was to find you.

01:39:22.660 --> 01:39:26.110
I remember that, too. Do you think I'd ever forget it?

01:39:35.920 --> 01:39:38.260
Uh, let's go find some place where we can get a drink, huh?

01:39:38.400 --> 01:39:39.440
Gotta wait for Johnny.

01:39:40.220 --> 01:39:41.080
We gotta wait for Johnny.

01:39:41.220 --> 01:39:45.540
What do you think I am, a camel?

01:39:45.720 --> 01:39:46.060
Come on.
